  "summary": "Proud U.S. Navy veteran, serve as an Electronics Technician Second Class, specializing in naval and satellite communications. After my years of service in the military I returned to college, and attended the Interamerican University of Puerto Rico to complete a second bachelors degree, this time in Computer Science. Currently I'm completing a M.S Computer Science in Software Engineering.\n\nI'm a Software Engineer with a U.S. Navy background and extensive experience delivering mission‑critical aerospace test solutions. Recognized twice for job‑scope advancement in Oct 26, 2024 and May 5, 2026 due to superior performance and leadership. Expert in C#, .NET, Python, LabVIEW, and TestStand, with a proven ability to lead distributed teams, streamline development pipelines, and produce high‑impact results under tight schedules. My work has been of a great impact to different programs. I have supported like GPS-III, ORION and NGI, and others I continue to supporting like GPS-IIIF and GeoXO.",
